            "review_title": "Review at Il Grillo",
            "review_text": "David J\n8 contributions\n0\nCozy, comfortable with good, traditional offerings.\nNov 2018 • Friends\nThere is both a ground floor and second floor dining area, both warm and comfortable. Traditional pastas and other Italian specialties fill the reasonably priced menu. A bruschetta was topped with a generous portion of chopped tomato and was crisp and tasty. My Caesar salad was OK but lacking in assertive flavors. Pasta with pepper and olive oil was perfectly cooked, ample and flavorful. My dining companion had pasta with salmon and was very happy with it. Both a white and red wine were offered by the glass and were quite acceptable. Espresso was deep and rich but lacked the creama that properly finishes it off. \nMy only complaint is every table has an ashtray, encouraging smoking in both it's dining areas. Why not set aside a place for non-smokers to enjoy their meal without the stench of nearby cigarettes.\nRead more\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 28, 2018",
            "rating": 5.0,
            "review_date": "2026-10-15",
            "travel_date": "Recent",
